    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37896" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάϊστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαϊω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>heard of, detected,</i> usu. c. part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐγένετο ἐργασμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐγένετο προδιδούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.128
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.74
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐγένετο ὑπὸ Καμβύσεω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.146
			</span></i>; <i>perceived,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ant.Lib.
				34.4
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Onat.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.1.39
			</span></i> (dub.).</div>
